# BOHEMIA SIDE QUEST — PLAYABLE .bq (canon machine layer)
# S15 — THE LIGHTS GO OUT AT NINE
# Shape: collective action / leverage. Faction wires: MOB, TRADES. Grounded in the
# real: every strike is paid for first by the people striking, and leverage that
# costs you nothing is not leverage, it is a request. The crew that keeps the
# marquee lit is the only reason the corner has a crowd, and the crowd is the only
# reason anybody eats, so the switch in their hand hurts them before it hurts him.
# Systems AS the mechanic: LIGHT IS TERRITORY (canon) and the mob owns the strip
# by owning what is lit; a dark marquee is a territorial act whether anyone throws
# a punch or not. No proper names. CLOUT rides the deed: a private rate nobody
# sees is #quiet, a rate posted on the wall for every crew in the valley is
# #notable, killing the lights on the busiest night is #reckless, and taking the
# owner's money to keep them on is #risky because the crew finds out and the crew
# is who you live beside.

# ---- QUESTBOOK STUDY CITATIONS (QUEST STUDY LAW, 7/26/26) -------------------
# The corpus this quest is actually built from. Every id below resolves in
# records/BOHEMIA_QUESTBOOK_LAW_INDEX.json (3,672 citable findings mined out of
# the 152 studied quests in questbook/), and gates/quest_study_gate.js verifies
# the id AND the quoted law title verbatim. A citation is a claim the machine
# can check, never a name-drop.
# @STUDY Q104.P3  W2/W4/W6 (they gave the murder a procedure + the election is a campaign against people + the death machine became an extortion racket — our FACTION WEB + standing + city-
#   applied: the crew did not riot, they built a demand and took five weeks to agree on it, and the procedure is what makes it real.
# @STUDY Q104.W6  THE DEATH MACHINE BECAME AN EXTORTION RACKET
#   applied: the owner does not care about the money; he cares that nobody ever finds out the corner can go dark.
# @STUDY Q092.W2  THE INSTITUTION IS THE MONSTER
#   applied: the two who asked before you are still here, one bought off and one working nights alone up a ladder.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

@QUEST   bq_lights_at_nine   The Lights Go Out At Nine
@ACT     2
@FACTION TRADES
@ONCE    true

@ROLE steward  REQ  faction=TRADES  speaks_for_the_crew=true
@ROLE owner    REQ  faction=MOB     owns_the_marquee=true

@STAGE 10
  @LOG The crew that keeps the marquee lit has not been paid in five weeks and is talking about the switch.
  @DO show_objective 10
@STAGE 20
  @LOG The owner knows what a dark corner costs him. So does the crew, and it costs them first.
  @DO show_objective 20
  @DO complete_objective 10
@STAGE 30 COMPLETE #quiet
  @LOG Settled it in a back room. The crew gets paid weekly, the lights never blinked, and nobody had to be seen losing.
  @DO faction TRADES +8
  @DO bond steward +15
  @DO complete_objective 20
@STAGE 31 COMPLETE #notable
  @LOG Got the rate painted on the wall by the door where every crew in the valley can read it. He hated the paint more than the number.
  @DO faction TRADES +12
  @DO faction MOB -5
  @DO set_flag rate_on_the_wall
  @DO complete_objective 20
@STAGE 32 COMPLETE #reckless
  @LOG Killed the marquee at nine on the fullest night of the week. Four blocks went dark and quiet and everybody learned exactly whose hand is on that switch.
  @DO faction MOB -12
  @DO faction_posture MOB +1
  @DO advance_territory
  @DO set_flag pulled_the_switch
  @DO complete_objective 20
@STAGE 33 COMPLETE #risky
  @LOG Took his money to keep the lights on and let the crew find out the slow way. The corner is bright and I walk the long way around it now.
  @DO faction MOB +12
  @DO bond steward -25
  @DO complete_objective 20
@STAGE 34 FAIL #quiet
  @LOG Nothing agreed. The crew broke up over it inside a month and the lights are run by two frightened kids who won't ask for anything.
  @DO faction TRADES -8

@OBJ 10  "Hear the crew out"          target=steward
@OBJ 20  "Settle the marquee"         target=owner

# =====================================================================
# THE ASK. Theme in the first line: the switch hurts them first and she
# says so before you can point it out.
# =====================================================================
@TALK crew  speaker=steward  entry=stage>=10,stage<20
  @SAY Five weeks. Everybody keeps saying the money is coming and the lights keep coming on anyway, which is the whole problem. #tired
  @SAY We have one thing. At nine, the marquee goes on, and the corner fills, and everybody on this side of the street eats off that crowd. Including us.
  @SAY So if we pull it, we starve first and he starves second. That's our great weapon. You see why I need somebody else in the room.
  @OPT "Then what do you actually want?"   [gate: none]  -> want
  @OPT "Why has nobody else asked him?"     [gate: none]  TRAP -> nobody
  @OPT "Pull it and see what he does."      [gate: none]  -> want
  @OPT "This is between you and him."       [gate: none]  -> END  @DO set_stage 34
  @OPT (let her get to it)                  [gate: none]  SILENCE -> want
  @NOVERB "Tell her to take it to the other crews first"
@END

@TALK want  speaker=steward
  @SAY Weekly, not whenever. That's it. That's the entire demand and it took us five weeks to agree on it. #tired
  @SAY How you get there's yours. Quiet is fine. Loud is fine. Just don't come back with a promise, we have a drawer full of those.
  @DO set_stage 20
@END

# THE TRAP: the answer names the two electricians who tried before you, and
# hearing it is the moment this stops being about money.
@TALK nobody  speaker=steward
  @SAY Two did. One took a private number and moved off the corner and doesn't drink with us anymore. #dread
  @SAY The other one asked in front of people. He still works. He works nights, alone, up the ladder, on the far side where nobody would see a fall.
  @OPT "Understood. What do you want?"     [gate: none]  -> want  @DO learn two_asked_before
  @OPT (say nothing and let it land)        [gate: none]  SILENCE -> want  @DO learn two_asked_before
@END

# =====================================================================
# THE ROOM. He is generous, personable, and completely clear that this is
# about who gets to be seen deciding. That is the real negotiation.
# =====================================================================
@TALK backroom  speaker=owner  entry=stage>=20
  @SAY The crew sent a stranger. That's smart, actually. A stranger can say a number without it being an insult. #flat
  @SAY Here is my position and it isn't the one you rehearsed. I don't care about the money. I have the money. I care that the corner never once goes dark, because the day it goes dark is the day somebody finds out it can.
  @SAY So. Say your number, and tell me who's allowed to see me agree to it.
  @OPT "Weekly. Quietly. Just us."          [gate: none]  -> quietdeal
  @OPT "Weekly. Painted on the wall."        [gate: none]  -> wall
  @OPT "Weekly, or it goes dark at nine."    [gate: none]  -> threat
  @OPT "What's it worth to keep them off the switch?"  [gate: none]  TRAP -> bribe
  @NOVERB "Tell him which crew members can be bought"
@END

@TALK quietdeal  speaker=owner
  @SAY Weekly, in an envelope, from a man who doesn't talk. Done, and it was done before you sat down. #flat
  @SAY Nobody sees me pay and nobody sees them win, and in twelve years that's the only kind of agreement that has never broken on me.
  @OPT "Then it's done."                   [gate: none]  -> END  @DO set_stage 30
  @OPT (shake his hand and leave)            [gate: none]  SILENCE -> END  @DO set_stage 30
@END

@TALK wall  speaker=owner
  @SAY On the wall. In paint. Where every crew in this valley walks past it on the way to work. #dread
  @SAY You understand that the number is cheap and the paint is expensive. Fine. I'd rather be the man who posted a rate than the man whose corner went dark. Barely.
  @OPT "Paint it."                          [gate: none]  -> END  @DO set_stage 31
  @OPT "No. Keep it between us."             [gate: none]  -> quietdeal
@END

@TALK threat  speaker=owner
  @SAY Then it goes dark, and four blocks go dark behind it, and everybody sees whose hand was on it. #dread
  @SAY I won't forget that and neither will anyone standing in the street at nine. Say it again and mean it, or take the envelope.
  @OPT "Nine o'clock. Watch."               [gate: none]  -> END  @DO set_stage 32
  @OPT (walk out and go to the switch)       [gate: none]  SILENCE -> END  @DO set_stage 32
  @OPT "Weekly, quietly. Nobody goes dark."   [gate: none]  -> quietdeal
@END

@TALK bribe  speaker=owner
  @SAY Ah. There it is, and you got there faster than most. #flat
  @SAY Enough that you wouldn't have to work a ladder again. The crew finds out eventually, they always do, and you keep living on their street with their money in your pocket.
  @OPT "I'll take it."                    [gate: none]  -> END  @DO set_stage 33
  @OPT "No. Weekly, for all of them."        [gate: none]  -> quietdeal
  @OPT (leave without answering)              [gate: none]  SILENCE -> quietdeal
@END
